<title>UK: Hozelock says current trading is strong.</title>
<headline>Hozelock says current trading is strong.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's Hozelock Group Plc, a garden equipment maker, said on Wednesday current trading was strong due to good weather and less of the country being hit by water restrictions than this time last year.</p>
<p>&quot;Trading since the end of March 1997 is substantially ahead of the equivalent period in 1996,&quot; it said in a statement.</p>
<p>Chief executive David Codling said the group was expecting to announce satisfactory interim results in May with pre-tax profits of over 3.0 million stg.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 4365</p>
</text>
